      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Do you want to come learn noble etiquette from me?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: I'm glad you came to find me, even if just a little.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Don't get the wrong idea, this is just basic noble etiquette.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Do you want to learn the power of magic?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: The power of magic exceeds your imagination.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Hey, what\u2019s up?"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: To get a bountiful catch, you must take care of the fishing gear.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: This town is close to the sea, so we often have seafood dishes.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "They say there are mermaids deep in the sea. I wonder if that\u2019s true."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "If you have time, you should learn how to fish. You\u2019ll learn a lot."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "What\u2019s the matter? Why did you come to me?"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: This town may be small, but it has a great port, with ships sailing back
        and forth between the continents.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: After years of drifting at sea, I really need to rest on land for a while.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: The sea holds many treasures, but it also has many risks.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: If you want to go to the sea, you can take my ship.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Looking for me? Is there anything I can do for you?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Sailing and traveling the world has always been my wish.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: The life on the sea is enchanting, but I still find this town quite nice.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Everyone is working hard, I can\u2019t slack off either."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Iwish I had my own ship.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019ll wait for your instructions."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Why pry into other people\u2019s secrets? As long as it doesn\u2019t harm
        anyone, it\u2019s fine."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Hello, what would you like to know?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "What would happen if all four seasons existed at the same time\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Do you need my help?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Although I still revere God, I\u2019d rather do other things."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Praying to God in battle doesn\u2019t work; we must rely on ourselves."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Iwonder if God can hear my heart and grant my wishes.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Whether you believe in God or not, you must uphold love and peace.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: What can I do for you?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Honestly, patrolling alone is quite boring. If someone would come talk
        to me, I\u2019d be happy."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019m happy to be of service to you."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Guarding the lady is my duty.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: In this town, I often think about the old master.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Looking back, it feels like it happened just yesterday. Back then, the
        lady was just a child\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: If there were more people to accompany the lady, she would probably be
        happier.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019ll do my best if there\u2019s anything you need."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Adish without seasoning is bland. Don\u2019t forget to buy seasonings."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Good equipment can greatly improve work efficiency. What do I need to do?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Imust raise Bradley to be a great man. That\u2019s the meaning of my life."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "When Bradley grows up a bit more, I\u2019ll let him choose his own path."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Hello, what can I do for you?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Sister should have a broader future, but she\u2019s stuck in this town\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: If I were stronger, my sister could pursue her dreams.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Can you help me? Encourage me to stay strong.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "If you\u2019re willing, you can always come find me and my sister."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Is there something you can\u2019t handle?"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Be careful, don\u2019t go too far. There are many monsters outside."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Iheard you\u2019ve been dealing with the monsters around the town. You\u2019re
        doing well."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Sorry for the poor hospitality, is there something you need?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019m happy to be with my mother and sister. I feel really blessed."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "If Dad were still here\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Imust support my family. Can you cheer me on?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Is there anything you need me to do?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Weaving is a magical skill that can turn the old into something new.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: If you want to learn weaving, I can teach you.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Sometimes, I worry about the lack of inheritance.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Rather than making money, I wish someone would carry on my skills.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Iknow more than you think. What do you need?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Sticking to one\u2019s opinions doesn\u2019t work. Only change can bring
        new opportunities."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Don\u2019t worry, your grandfather just went to the place he wanted."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Live well here. Your grandfather will be very pleased.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Ididn\u2019t find what I wanted. I\u2019m a little upset."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Your team is already full. Let\u2019s talk about it next time."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "My body hasn\u2019t fully recovered yet. Let\u2019s try again another
        day."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019m going to rest at home now. Take care of yourself."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "The Creator hasn\u2019t yet created this kind of relationship. Please
        wait patiently."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Sorry, we\u2019re not close enough to form a team yet."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Not yet, you need to work harder to earn my trust.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Istill have things to do, I can\u2019t join you in the team."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "If we get closer, I\u2019ll agree."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Sorry, I can\u2019t go out with you right now."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Ineed to train my willpower. If you can change me, maybe it\u2019ll work."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Ican\u2019t fully trust you yet."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Can I trust you to watch my back? Probably not.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "As a good captain, you need to choose your team wisely. You\u2019re not
        ready yet."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Sorry, I\u2019m not used to working with strangers."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Sorry, my time is valuable. You need to earn my trust first.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Ineed to look after the young lady, unless we become closer.
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "I\u2019m glad you invited me, but please allow me to refuse."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "My duties are very important. Unless you can prove you\u2019re more important."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Our relationship isn\u2019t close enough yet. I can\u2019t agree to that."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Ah, this\u2026 thank you anyway."
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "If it\u2019s\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Idon\u2019t really need this\u2026"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Hmm, can we exchange it for something else next time?
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Wow, what a great gift! Thank you!
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: "Is this for me? I\u2019m so happy!"
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Exactly what I needed! Thank you!
      jp: 
      ko: 
    - en: Thanks for the gift!
      jp: 
      ko: 
